Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Uncluttered play view without the top-left website logo.
Dependencies: Completed workstreams 18 and 29.

Purpose:
Remove the website wordmark in game view without hiding notifications, changing
the handheld, or removing the logo from the desk, inspection or startup screen.

Tasks:
- [x] Bind header wordmark visibility to the existing settled playing view.
- [x] Preserve header layout so notifications do not jump or lose their safe fit.
- [x] Extend responsive branding coverage with pickup/inspect/put-down transitions.
- [x] Document the view-specific behavior and preserve the causal ledger.
- [ ] Complete focused checks, publish normally and independently verify live.

Acceptance criteria:
- The top-left wordmark is hidden in playing mode at desktop and phone widths.
- Table and Inspect retain the wordmark; returning to play hides it again.
- Header notices remain visible and clear of the actual handheld.
- Startup and physical/fullscreen bezel branding remain unchanged.
- Existing release gates stay intact; publication is not inferred from local tests.

Completion evidence:
- CSS uses the existing scene data-view; no new application state or event handler.
- visibility:hidden retains the header box and its notification positioning.
- Validation and publication outcomes are recorded below when observed.
- Syntax/build, all 11 units and three focused Edge cases pass in 1.0m.
  Desktop/phone transitions, actual notice visibility, five-size clearance and
  whole-handheld/power containment pass. Actual 1920px play capture reviewed.
  Hosted release and independent public verification remain pending.

Completion log:
- 2026-11-04: User requests hiding the upper-left website logo in game view.
  Add a play-only CSS rule and extend existing browser cases rather than
  remove the complete heading/notice host or alter camera/runtime behavior.
